      *>--- conformance-case
      *> id: pb2635_nan_selection_agrees_with_ordinal
      *> rules: [RV-15.59.4-1, RV-15.63.4-1, RV-15.71.4-1, RV-15.71.4-3, RV-15.72.4-1, RV-15.72.4-3]
      *> accept: [2014, 2023]
      *> source-format: fixed
      *> portable: unverified
      *>---
       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
       PROGRAM-ID. PB2635NAN.
      *> KB/WORK PB2635: MAX AND MIN RETURN "THE CONTENT OF THE
      *> ARGUMENT-1 HAVING THE GREATEST [LEAST] VALUE" (15.59.4 RV1,
      *> 15.63.4 RV1) AND ORD-MAX AND ORD-MIN THE POSITION OF THAT
      *> SAME ARGUMENT, THE LEFTMOST ON A TIE (15.71.4 RV1, RV3;
      *> 15.72.4 RV1, RV3). ONE SELECTION RULE SERVES ALL FOUR, SO A
      *> VALUE AND ITS ORDINAL NAME ONE ARGUMENT. A NAN IS UNORDERED:
      *> NO COMPARISON MAKES IT GREATER OR LESS THAN 1, SO THE
      *> LEFTMOST ARGUMENT STAYS SELECTED. BEFORE PB2635 THE BINARY64
      *> MAX AND MIN USED A SECOND RULE: MIN (Y X) SELECTED THE NAN
      *> WHILE ORD-MIN (Y X) NAMED Y. THE SELECTED NAN'S OWN LANDING
      *> (MAX (X Y), MIN (X Y)) IS KB/WORK PB6042'S, NOT
      *> PINNED HERE.
       DATA DIVISION.
       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
       01 B PIC X(8).
       01 X REDEFINES B USAGE FLOAT-BINARY-64.
       01 Y USAGE FLOAT-BINARY-64 VALUE 1.
       01 S USAGE FLOAT-BINARY-64.
       01 N PIC 9.
       PROCEDURE DIVISION.
           MOVE X"7FF8000000000000" TO B.
           IF X IS FLOAT-NOT-A-NUMBER DISPLAY "X IS NAN" END-IF.
           COMPUTE S = FUNCTION MAX (Y X).
           DISPLAY "MAX (Y X) " S.
           COMPUTE S = FUNCTION MIN (Y X).
           DISPLAY "MIN (Y X) " S.
           MOVE FUNCTION ORD-MAX (Y X) TO N.
           DISPLAY "ORD-MAX (Y X) " N.
           MOVE FUNCTION ORD-MIN (Y X) TO N.
           DISPLAY "ORD-MIN (Y X) " N.
           MOVE FUNCTION ORD-MAX (X Y) TO N.
           DISPLAY "ORD-MAX (X Y) " N.
           MOVE FUNCTION ORD-MIN (X Y) TO N.
           DISPLAY "ORD-MIN (X Y) " N.
           STOP RUN.
